# Episode 6: Claude Code Deep Dive for DevOps
# AI-Assisted DevOps Workshop
# Author: Sagar Utekar
#
# Prerequisites:
#   - Claude Code installed (npm install -g @anthropic-ai/claude-code)
#   - ANTHROPIC_API_KEY environment variable set
#
# Usage:
#   Copy this file to your project root as CLAUDE.md (remove the .example extension).
#   Claude Code reads it automatically when you run `claude` in that directory.

# Project: Production Infrastructure

## Environment
- Kubernetes: EKS 1.29, 3 node groups (general/memory/gpu)
- Service Mesh: Istio 1.20
- Monitoring: Prometheus + Grafana + Loki
- CI/CD: GitHub Actions + ArgoCD
- Secrets: HashiCorp Vault
- IaC: Terraform 1.7 with S3 backend

## Conventions
- All K8s manifests use Kustomize (not Helm) for our custom apps
- Terraform modules are in `terraform/modules/`
- Environment-specific configs in `terraform/envs/{dev,staging,prod}/`
- All deployments must have resource limits, health checks, and PDBs
- Images come from our ECR: 123456789.dkr.ecr.us-east-1.amazonaws.com

## Namespaces
- `production` — Live traffic (be VERY careful)
- `staging` — Pre-prod testing
- `monitoring` — Prometheus, Grafana, Loki
- `istio-system` — Service mesh control plane

## On-Call Runbooks
- Pod CrashLoopBackOff: Check logs → Check resources → Check config maps → Rollback if recent deploy
- High Latency: Check Istio → Check upstream → Check HPA → Check node resources
- Node Not Ready: Check kubelet → Check disk pressure → Check network → Drain if needed

## Safety Rules
- NEVER run kubectl delete on production namespace without asking me first
- NEVER modify istio-system resources
- Always use --dry-run=client before applying changes
- Terraform: always plan before apply
